	(text_box "I_LED = VA1 / 10 Ω = 0 to 48 mA, linear in the DAC code.\nDC coupled: a code of 8192 is a 24 mA bias, and a sine on top of it is intensity modulation.\nJP2009 picks the on-board red LED (625 nm) or your own on J210 (anode to +5 V, cathode to the driver).\nBandwidth is set by the transistor and the OPA2810: a few MHz."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 299.72 299.72 0)
		(size 92.71 8.89)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 194 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.95 0.95)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "78ae4dff-fba7-b2f6-13cd-2bfcedf4b6fb")
	)
	(text_box "Timing: data is latched by WRT and the DAC updates on CLK; tie them to the same FPGA clock for the simple case.\n14 bits at 125 MSPS, straight binary (code 0 = IOUTA off = -2 V unloaded)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 340.36 0)
		(size 99.06 6.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 194 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.95 0.95)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "9d1f2ce9-b479-a1e4-9e68-6143a7b0747a")
	)
	(text_box "The FPGA writes 14 bits per port with its own WRT and CLK (dual-port mode; drive MODE low and the same four pins become IQWRT/IQCLK/IQRESET/IQSEL for interleaved I/Q).\nEach DAC sources 0-19.2 mA into 24.9 Ω on complementary outputs;\nan OPA2810 takes the difference with gain 4.4: ±2 V unloaded, ±1 V into 50 Ω, DC coupled, centred on 0 V.\nChannel 1's unipolar node also feeds a voltage-to-current stage that drives an LED (on board, or your own on J210) for the optical experiments."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 25.4 0)
		(size 172.72 10.16)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 194 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.1 1.1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d7640c1c-0bcb-aa9b-4249-3c0e776b42b9")
	)
